id: pm-gh1702
title: "GH-1702: pm test --run prints the full execution_context with host paths on every passing run; default to the lean projection"
description: "GH-1702 (filed 2026-11-11). pm test --run prints the full 21-field linked-test execution_context on every run, including a single passing test: sandbox and source tracker paths, counts, seeding flags, the trust fingerprint and the working directory. Two of those are absolute host paths: the global tracker under the caller's home directory, and the caller's checkout. Measured on a fresh tracker with one passing test: default TOON 1,975 B with 1,217 B of context (62 percent), --json 2,479 B with 1,355 B, --lean 798 B with 236 B. Agents paste this output into comments and PR text as evidence, so the default form carries host paths into public text and trips privacy gates. pm-fqdmbf hoisted the block across tests but a single-test item still pays it. Proposal: the lean five-field context (pm_context_mode, workspace_context_mode, mismatch_detected, trusted, trust_reason) becomes the default for TOON and JSON; the full block prints only when it explains something (mismatch, trust or config refusal, non-passing result, or an explicit request) with the existing restore hint; no absolute path outside the tracker in the default projection."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"gh:1702",linked-tests,privacy,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-11-12T05:13:29.775Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-13T09:29:29.562Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-13T08:40:45.891Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-13T08:40:45.891Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "The default TOON and JSON pm test --run output carries only the five decision fields of execution_context when nothing needs explaining; The full context prints on a mismatch, a trust or config refusal, a non-passing result, or an explicit request, with the restore hint; The default projection prints no absolute path outside the tracker"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "projectLinkedTestEvidence (src/core/output/output.ts) applies the decision-context projection to every quiet success, not only under --lean: pm_context_mode, workspace_context_mode, mismatch_detected, trusted, trust_reason and restore_with naming --check-context. Failures, refusals, skips, mismatches and non-zero failure categories keep the full hoisted block. --check-context is the explicit request (no new flag); its help text says so. Lean and default share one predicate. Declared as contract_change with a migration line. Follow-up pm-tcvccz covers pm test-all."
expected_result: A passing single-test run prints a small context with no host paths
actual_result: "Fresh sandbox, one passing test: default TOON 2,033 -> 965 B, JSON 2,525 -> 1,360 B, zero absolute paths; --check-context keeps all four tracker paths; failure variants keep the full block in lean and default (output.spec.ts), integration spec reads trusted/trust_reason from the default receipt"
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
