comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-13T07:56:58.471Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence (2026-11-13, branch feat/default-output-economy): projectLinkedTestEvidence now reduces a quiet success (ok, all rows passed, no mismatch, no non-zero failure category) to the decision context in every format, not only under --lean. --check-context is the explicit full-context request, chosen over a new flag because it already means 'check the PM context' and adds no packaged bytes or replication-set rows; its help text now says it reports the full context. Measured on a fresh sandbox tracker, one passing test: default TOON 2,033 -> 965 B, JSON 2,525 -> 1,360 B, zero absolute paths in either; --lean 763 -> 769 B (hint text). Lean and default share one predicate, so an untrusted pass under --allow-untrusted-linked-tests keeps trusted:false and trust_reason. Found pm test-all has the same defect on every row and filed pm-tcvccz."
  "2026-11-13T09:03:27.618Z","harness:claude-code","Review fix (Greptile P2 on PR 1720, 2026-11-13): the first implementation reduced the context only after hoisting a shared full context, and linkedTestTrustFingerprint includes the command, so any item with two different linked tests never shared a full context and kept every path on every row. projectLinkedTestEvidence now reduces each quiet row to its decision fields first and then hoists the identical result; rows whose decision fields differ (for example different trust reasons) keep their own reduced contexts. Measured on the sandbox item with two passing tests: TOON 2,733 -> 1,078 B, zero absolute paths. New spec case in output.spec.ts covers differing fingerprints, differing trust reasons, a row without a context and an empty run."
